st my husband will become attached to me, because I have borne him three sons.” So he was named Levi.","from":47},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the man said, “Your name will no longer be Jacob, but Israel, because you have struggled with God and with men, and you have prevailed.”","from":38},{"book":"GEN","chapter":36,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and Oholibamah gave birth to Jeush, Jalam, and Korah. These were the sons of Esau, who were born to him in the land of Canaan.","from":37},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.","from":38},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.","from":47}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":3},{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2},{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"49-53":{"people":[{"id":"aaron-h0175","name":"Aaron","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":2,"firstVerse":49},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":49},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"firstVerse":49},{"id":"abishua-h0050g","name":"Abishua","kind":"person","brief":"A priest","count":1,"firstVerse":50},{"id":"eleazar-h0499g","name":"Eleazar","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":50},{"id":"phinehas-h6372g","name":"Phinehas","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":50},{"id":"bukki-h1231h","name":"Bukki","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":51},{"id":"uzzi-h5813g","name":"Uzzi","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":51},{"id":"zerahiah-h2228g","name":"Zerahiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":51},{"id":"ahitub-h0285h","name":"Ahitub","kind":"person","brief":"A priest","count":1,"firstVerse":52},{"id":"amariah-h0568g","name":"Amariah","kind":"person","brief":"A priest","count":1,"firstVerse":52},{"id":"meraioth-h4812g","name":"Meraioth","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":52},{"id":"ahimaaz-h0290h","name":"Ahimaaz","kind":"person","brief":"A priest","count":1,"firstVerse":53},{"id":"zadok-h6659g","name":"Zadok","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":53}],"places":[{"id":"most-holy-place-h6944h","name":"Most Holy Place","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":49}],"words":[{"base":"H0175","lemma":"אַהֲרֹן","tr":"a·ha·ron","gloss":"Aaron","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":347},{"base":"H4196","lemma":"מִזְבֵּחַ","tr":"miz·be·ach","gloss":"altar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":401},{"base":"H6944","lemma":"קֹ֫דֶשׁ","tr":"qo·desh","gloss":"holiness","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":469},{"base":"H0050","lemma":"אֲבִישׁוּעַ","tr":"a·vi·shu·a","gloss":"Abishua","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H1231","lemma":"בֻּקִּי","tr":"buq·qi","gloss":"Bukki","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H2228","lemma":"זְרַחְיָה","tr":"ze·rach·yah","gloss":"Zerahiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H4812","lemma":"מְרָיוֹת","tr":"me·ra·vot","gloss":"Meraioth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H5813","lemma":"עֻזִּי","tr":"uz·zi","gloss":"Uzzi","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H0285","lemma":"אֲחִיטוּב","tr":"a·chi·tuv","gloss":"Ahitub","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H0290","lemma":"אֲחִימַ֫עַץ","tr":"a·chi·ma·ats","gloss":"Ahimaaz","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LEV","chapter":4,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"He shall offer this bull just as he did the bull for the sin offering; in this way the priest will make atonement on their behalf, and they will be forgiven.","from":49},{"book":"EXO","chapter":6,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Aaron married Elisheba, the daughter of Amminadab and sister of Nahshon, and she bore him Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar.","from":50},{"book":"EXO","chapter":27,"verse":1,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“You are to build an altar of acacia wood. The altar must be square, five cubits long, five cubits wide, and three cubits high. Make a horn on each of its four corners, so that the horns are of one piece, and overlay it with bronze. Make all its utensils of bronze—its pots for removing ashes, its shovels, its sprinkling bowls, its meat forks, and its firepans. Construct for it a grate of bronze mesh, and make a bronze ring at each of the four corners of the mesh. Set the grate beneath the ledge of the altar, so that the mesh comes halfway up the altar.","from":49},{"book":"EXO","chapter":28,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“Next, have your brother Aaron brought to you from among the Israelites, along with his sons Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar, to serve Me as priests.","from":50},{"book":"EXO","chapter":29,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They must eat those things by which atonement was made for their ordination and consecration. But no outsider may eat them, because these things are sacred.","from":49},{"book":"EXO","chapter":29,"verse":36,"verseEnd":37,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Sacrifice a bull as a sin offering each day for atonement. Purify the altar by making atonement for it, and anoint it to consecrate it. For seven days you shall make atonement for the altar and consecrate it. Then the altar will become most holy; whatever touches the altar will be holy.","from":49},{"book":"EXO","chapter":30,"verse":1,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“You are also to make an altar of acacia wood for the burning of incense. It is to be square, a cubit long, a cubit wide, and two cubits high. Its horns must be of one piece. Overlay with pure gold the top and all the sides and horns, and make a molding of gold around it. And make two gold rings below the molding on opposite sides to hold the poles used to carry it. Make the poles of acacia wood and overlay them with gold.","from":49},{"book":"EXO","chapter":30,"verse":10,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Once a year Aaron shall make atonement on the horns of the altar. Throughout your generations he shall make atonement on it annually with the blood of the sin offering of atonement. The altar is most holy to the LORD.” Then the LORD said to Moses, “When you take a census of the Israelites to number them, each man must pay the LORD a ransom for his life when he is counted. Then no plague will come upon them when they are numbered. Everyone who crosses over to those counted must pay a half shekel, according to the sanctuary shekel, which weighs twenty gerahs. This half shekel is an offering to the LORD. Everyone twenty years of age or older who crosses over must give this offering to the LORD.","from":49}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":3}]},"54-81":{"people":[{"id":"kohath-h6955","name":"Kohath","kind":"person","brief":"Levi's son","count":4,"firstVerse":54},{"id":"aaron-h0175","name":"Aaron","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":2,"firstVerse":54},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":55},{"id":"caleb-h3612g","name":"Caleb","kind":"person","brief":"Joshua's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":56},{"id":"jephunneh-h3312g","name":"Jephunneh","kind":"