age":42,"uses":115},{"base":"H4294","lemma":"מַטֶּה","tr":"mat·teh","gloss":"tribe: rod","lang":"h","inPassage":22,"uses":252},{"base":"H5892","lemma":"עִיר","tr":"ir","gloss":"excitement","lang":"h","inPassage":11,"uses":1090},{"base":"H4940","lemma":"מִשְׁפָּחָה","tr":"mish·pa·chah","gloss":"family","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":303},{"base":"H1486","lemma":"גּוֹרָל","tr":"go·ral","gloss":"allotted","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":77},{"base":"H4519","lemma":"מְנַשֶּׁה","tr":"me·nash·sheh","gloss":"Manasseh","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":146},{"base":"H6955","lemma":"קְהָת","tr":"qe·hat","gloss":"Kohath","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":32},{"base":"H7216","lemma":"רָאמוֹת","tr":"ra·mot","gloss":"Ramoth","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H3498","lemma":"יָתַר","tr":"ya·tar","gloss":"to remain","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":106},{"base":"H1667","lemma":"גַּת־רִמּוֹן","tr":"gat-rim·mon","gloss":"Gath-rimmon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":21,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"This is what the Levite clans of the Gershonites were given: From the half-tribe of Manasseh they were given Golan in Bashan, a city of refuge for the manslayer, and Beeshterah—two cities, together with their pasturelands.","from":71},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"These were the sons of Ishmael, and these were their names by their villages and encampments—twelve princes of their tribes.","from":54},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Jacob saw them, he said, “This is the camp of God.” So he named that place Mahanaim.","from":80},{"book":"GEN","chapter":33,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"After Jacob had come from Paddan-aram, he arrived safely at the city of Shechem in the land of Canaan, and he camped just outside the city.","from":67},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So they gave Jacob all their foreign gods and all their earrings, and Jacob buried them under the oak near Shechem.","from":67},{"book":"GEN","chapter":46,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.","from":63},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And she gave birth to a son, and Moses named him Gershom, saying, “I have become a foreigner in a foreign land.”","from":62},{"book":"NUM","chapter":3,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the sons of Merari by their clans were Mahli and Mushi. These were the clans of the Levites, according to their families.","from":63}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":11},{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":3}]}}